\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let $M$ be a smooth projective complex variety of dimension $n$, $L$ an ample line bundle, and $K_M$ the canonical line bundle. Must $K_M\otimes L^{\otimes m}$ be globally generated for $m\geq n+1$ and very ample for $m\geq n+2$?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=List_of_unsolved_problems_in_mathematics&oldid=1366636767#Geometry}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let $M$ be a smooth projective complex variety of dimension $n$, $L$ an ample line bundle, and $K_M$ the canonical line bundle. Must $K_M\otimes L^{\otimes m}$ be globally generated for $m\geq n+1$ and very ample for $m\geq n+2$?

